Prestige nostalgia is missing what a time made you in other people’s eyes. You hear an old nickname and, for a second, you’re back in a room where everyone knows what you’ve done and why they want you there.

It can also work with a past you never lived. You put on an old flight jacket and borrow a little of the regard that once came with wearing it. To the person who wore it every day, it might have meant another shift. To you, it carries the romance of a whole era. One generation’s work clothes become another generation’s costume of distinction.

That brings it back to what a title affords. The jacket can bring back how it felt to be somebody. The deeper question is what did that room let me do or be that I still want now? Sometimes what you miss most is being counted on by people you counted on, too.